Z||000006||Her86GT||12-14-2001||06:41 PM||||Maybe you should really get to know her first.  Usually girls who are attractive are fairly causious about just going out on a date with someone they barely know.  Alot of guys see a good looking chick and think it's an easy lay.  I speak from experience on this one.  I'm just being honest.  Girls have to be alot more careful than guys when it comes to dating people they don't really know.  Being that there is date rape drugs out there and stuff of the like.  Us girls have to be careful!  I'm not trying to depress you but do yourself and her a favour and do the homework and get to really know her to gain trust.  I like it when guys talk with me in an invironment that I'm familiar with.  Going out for a coffee or something very simple.  You do know that she knows you like her by now so keep it simple. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar2sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-14-2001||09:00 PM||||At school last winter, I met this girl, and started getting to know her.. she was absolutely perfect, except for she smoked, and drank a lot, was very religious, and a bit obsessive... (but not about me. dammit..)<BR>she looked like Alexandra Holden.. (Fern, the gun dealer's daughter, from the movie Sugar & Spice)<P>I asked her if she wanted to go hang out at the mall sometime, she said she was busy that weekend.. but she wanted me to call her.. so I did. we talked a few times after that, she always told me to call her back again, after we talked for a while.. anyway, one time I called her and she seemed sorta distant, and just before she hung up, she said "maybe I'll see you around school sometime."<P>I took that as meaning "go away.", so I did.. I didn't call her again. that proved to be a BIG mistake, cause 3 months later I found out she was still single, thought that no one liked her, and wondered why I just stopped calling.. that was the day before I moved back home for the summer.<P>I can't believe I lost her like that, she was one of the most bautiful girls I've ever known.. the first night I met her, she'd just been rudely dumped by her bf (his idea of how to dump a girl? arrange to have her walk in on him and his new gf...) anyway, we talked for hours, and then went to the mall.. she was cold.. I gave her my sweater and coat.. it was slippery out, I held onto her when we walked across some ice patches.. and she loved the little teddy bear and rose I got her for valentines day. my sister met her when she was visiting, and she said this girl was starting to like me... and I f*cked it up.<P>anyway, I'm in no position to give advice.. but here's some anyway.. don't scare her off (I've done that to girls befor.. now I'm too shy to say much of anything...) but don't give up right away either... you might regret what might have been.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||9
